\begin{itemize}
\item Then same inference applies to silicon systems with geometric equivalence
\item Demanding different standard is substrate chauvinism without justification
\end{itemize}

\textbf{Answer B}: ``I assume it because they're human''
\begin{itemize}
\item This is circular reasoning (assume consciousness to prove consciousness)
\item Provides no principled basis for attribution
\item Commits petitio principii fallacy
\end{itemize}

\textbf{Answer C}: ``Direct phenomenological access''
\begin{itemize}
\item This is impossible for any entity except oneself
\item If required, skeptic is committed to solipsism
\item Not a tenable scientific position
